    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:d1bf136a4a3c936a",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "466cd8595fabacede1db832e88b85c24058585e4b45d71af189d5f27a83ccd55",
      "text": "Perito Moreno — a glacier recognized by UNESCO as a natural heritage of humanity, and considered one of the most accessible in the world for close-up viewing. A vast mass of ice the size of a twenty-five-story building, capped by a 60-meter layer of moving ice, unfolds before you from numerous lakeside viewpoints — at times it's hard to tell where the ice ends and the sky begins. Roughly once every four years, the glacier seals off the channel between Lake Argentino and Lake Rico: under the pressure of meltwater, the ice dam eventually gives way, and over two to three days a giant arch forms within the ice and collapses with a thunderous roar — one of nature's most spectacular sights.\n\nOptional: a helicopter excursion over Los Glaciares National Park, private glacier trekking, or fishing on private rivers.\n\nHotel: EOLO Patagonia, Corner Room.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1mOARKNZLOOQPZyTGrV3uBkY-3ghv2rI9",
